post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> ultranix-mcp installed. Binary: /usr/bin/ultranix-mcp

    Optional - uinput/evdev input fallback (NOT needed on Hyprland/wlroots,
    where the compositor-native backends require no elevated permissions).
    The packaged udev rule is opt-in: it does nothing until the dedicated
    group exists and the service user joins it. See
    /usr/share/doc/ultranix-mcp/README-uinput.md:

      sudo groupadd ultranix-input
      sudo usermod -aG ultranix-input <service-user>
      echo uinput | sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/uinput.conf
      sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
      sudo udevadm trigger --name-match=uinput

    Then re-login so group membership takes effect.

    For HTTP daemon mode (:3010) the user unit is packaged at
    /usr/lib/systemd/user/ultranix-mcp.service - configure
    %h/.config/ultranix-mcp/env with ULTRANIX_MCP_API_KEY first, then:

      systemctl --user daemon-reload
      systemctl --user enable --now ultranix-mcp.service
EOF
}
